{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033943-hack-refine","id":1033943,"title":"[Hack] Refine","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-18T03:45:38-08:00","id":1033943,"title":"[Hack] Refine","content":"Mage 2E made a lot of positive changes, Reach being one of them. It managed to condense the spell list, provided greater clarification of what spells did because they could be constrained to the Practices without their effects being too limited, and allowed Paradox to truly become the rope that mages hang themselves with. That said, it does have some limitations. Some spells still are duplicated into more advanced Practices. I fully understand why the developers did this, Reach doesn't provide hard limitations and sometimes you need that, but it still kinda flies in the face of what Reach was supposed to do. That, and it kinda sucks to have more than one Rote for one spell.<br /> <br /> That's why I came up with Refine. From a mage's perspective, Reaching is simply adding more power to the equation, Refining is using a more complex formula to begin with. They cast the same spell with the same general effect, but with a more advanced Practice for a greater effect.<br /> <br /> When Refined, a spell is considered to be of the new Practice\u2019s dot level for all purposes (determining free Reach, Withstanding dispellation, etc.). The caster can use Reach effects from a lower Practice so long as they use the Reach for it (although for most spells you probably wouldn\u2019t want to do it, but it is optional).<br /> <br /> A spell can be Refined into multiple Practices so long as they keep to the general effect and each one is higher than the last. This means a single spell can be Refined by 4 Practices (at least where mages are concerned). I don\u2019t really expect something like that to happen, though.<br /> <br /> If a Refined spell would change any elements of the spell on the last lower Practice, such as the Primary Spell Factor, being Withstood (or not Withstood), and the like must be noted. Otherwise, assume it\u2019s the same as the last lower Practice.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Example Spells</b></u><br /> <br /> Instead of Rotting Flesh and Withering, there's-<br /> <br /> <u><b>Rot (Death \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)</b></u><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Perfecting<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> From the moment of birth, Death begins its slow, patient work. The caster simply commands it to hasten that work on the subject. Old wounds peel open, organs slow to a crawl, and disease ravishes the system, dealing 1 bashing for every level of Potency.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The spell makes the subject\u2019s rot painfully obvious. If targeting a living subject, the caster may inflict a penalty on all their Social rolls equal to Potency (to a limit of -3).<br /> <b>Refine to Patterning (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf):</b> The subject curdles into an icon of Death as blood floods out, bones erode, and the body withers. Each level of Potency deals 1 lethal damage.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> By spending 1 Mana, the caster deals aggravated damage instead.<br /> <br /> Instead of Influence Fire and Control Fire there's-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Wield Flames (Forces \u25cf)</u><br /> Practice:</b> Compelling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> Humanity\u2019s dominance over the natural world began with its mastery of fire. The mage takes this mastery to a whole new level by directing its course any way they see fit, even make firey shapes from it. Until the end of the spell\u2019s Duration, the mage can direct the fire anywhere within sensory range (including remote viewing) at a Speed of Gnosis + Forces. They must take an action to direct it (casting the spell counts as directing it). Should the mage stop or be stopped while directing it, the fire hangs, even in the middle of the air. While the mage cannot increase or decrease the flame\u2019s intensity, but they can direct it to a source of fuel or into something inflammable like water.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Through efficient direction, the mage can increase or decrease<br /> <b>Refine to Ruling (\u25cf\u25cf):</b> In addition to moving them, the mage can make the flames roar or dampen for as long as the Duration lasts. Each level of Potency can either add to the heat or size of the fire by one level, or subtract the heat or size by one level. If the fire\u2019s heat or size is reduced to zero, the fire is extinguished until the Duration ends.<br /> <b>Refine to Perfecting/Fraying (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)<br /> Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> The increase or decrease of the fire\u2019s heat and size become Lasting, as the mage truly fuels or depletes the flames.<br /> <br /> Discussion and criticisms are all welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T04:15:47-08:00","id":1033947,"title":"","content":"Rot: Death can already do that without claiming that its been pushed back to a later level unnecessarily, it just can't do Lethal. Creative Thaumaturgy yo.<br /> <br /> Wield Flames: Clearly a Ruling effect that you've decided to &quot;downgrade&quot; to Compelling despite the fact that you're clearly including Ruling (or higher) effects for reasons that I don't understand.<br /> <br /> Basically, I don't see this actually adding anything and I'm not sure you understand what the various Practices do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T11:37:49-08:00","id":1034136,"title":"","content":"So, given the &quot;level&quot; is unchanged (thus, when Mages get access to it, and what Reach they are given freely), the main effect this has is so that Praxis, Rotes, and anything else that is tied to a single &quot;spell&quot; is more widely applicable? IE, A Praxis for the 3-dot Bashing Damage attack spell also applies to the 4-dot Lethal (or Aggravated) version once the Mage gets access to that level of Arcana?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T14:28:22-08:00","id":1034246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033943-hack-refine?p=1033947#post1033947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rot: Death can already do that without claiming that its been pushed back to a later level unnecessarily, it just can't do Lethal. Creative Thaumaturgy yo.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the only difference between Rotting Flesh and Withering is the type of damage they do, why not condense it into 1 spell? That's what Refine is meant to do, condensing the spell list by providing the hard limitation that Reach cannot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033943-hack-refine?p=1033947#post1033947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wield Flames: Clearly a Ruling effect that you've decided to &quot;downgrade&quot; to Compelling despite the fact that you're clearly including Ruling (or higher) effects for reasons that I don't understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Influence Fire is a Compelling spell that allows you to move fire around, it's in the corebook on p.140. I referenced the spell in the OP, even.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033943-hack-refine?p=1033947#post1033947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, I don't see this actually adding anything and I'm not sure you understand what the various Practices do.</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, Refine is meant to condense spells with similar effects together, so by nature it doesn't add much. That said, I'm sure plenty of players would appreciate not having to purchase as many Rotes/Praxes. Second, you might as well be saying the developers don't understand the Practices, because I've been referencing the spells they wrote.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033943-hack-refine?p=1034136#post1034136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, given the &quot;level&quot; is unchanged (thus, when Mages get access to it, and what Reach they are given freely), the main effect this has is so that Praxis, Rotes, and anything else that is tied to a single &quot;spell&quot; is more widely applicable? IE, A Praxis for the 3-dot Bashing Damage attack spell also applies to the 4-dot Lethal (or Aggravated) version once the Mage gets access to that level of Arcana?</div> </div> </div> </div>Essentially, yes. Though when Refined, the spell's dot level does change to the higher Practice's level, so calculating free Reach, Withstanding dispellation, etc. does change.<br /> <br /> Basically, if a mage with 3 dots in Death decides to purchase Rot as a Rote, they can later Refine the spell to do lethal/aggravated damage once they hit Death 4, rather than having to purchase two Rotes for Rotting Flesh (3-dot Death that does bashing) and Withering (4-dot Death that does lethal/aggravated).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T14:36:37-08:00","id":1034250,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2992\" data-vbnamecard=\"2992\">crapcarp</a> How does this interact with Artifacts, Imbued items, and Proximus Blessings?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T15:18:50-08:00","id":1034280,"title":"","content":"I see that I misread what the intention of the thread was. My bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T17:13:01-08:00","id":1034337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033943-hack-refine?p=1034250#post1034250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2992\" data-vbnamecard=\"2992\">crapcarp</a> How does this interact with Artifacts, Imbued items, and Proximus Blessings?</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually didn't think of that, so thank you for bringing that to my attention.<br /> <br /> <b>Artifacts:</b> Spells can come already Refined, in which case they are considered to be at the higher dot level for determining the Merit's dots. The mage wielding them can Refine any of the Artifact's spells, so long as they have the right Arcanum dots and they must use their own Arcanum rating (they can use the Artifact's Gnosis, though).<br /> <br /> For example, an Artifact that takes the form of a skull with ruby eyes has both Rot and Wield Flames. Both spells can already be Refined by default, so let's say both spells have been Refined to the highest Practice (so it costs 6 dots). The Artifact's Arcanum rating would be 4, the same as Rot when Refined to Patterning, and therefore would have 1 free Reach for it and 2 free Reach for Wield Flames. Now let's say both Rot and Wield Flames are not Refined, so the Arcanum rating would be 3, with Rot having 1 free Reach and Wield Flames having 3. Let's say the mage wielding it has Death 3 and Forces 2, this means that the mage cannot Refine Rot to the higher Practice, but they can Refine Wield Flames to the Ruling Practice.<br /> <br /> <b>Imbued Items:</b> Spells must come already Refined. They cannot be Refined further even if the mage has enough Arcanum dots. For example, an item Imbued with Rot at 3 dots cannot be Refined to Patterning even if the mage has Death 4.<br /> <br /> <b>Proximus Blessings:</b> Much like Imbued Item, and spells used for Blessings can only be Refined up to 3 dot Practices. This means that Rot Refined to Patterning cannot be used as a Blessing, but Wield Flames can be Refined up to Perfecting/Fraying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033943-hack-refine?p=1034280#post1034280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see that I misread what the intention of the thread was. My bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's all good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T01:20:57-08:00","id":1036493,"title":"","content":"Interesting approach. However, I'd actually make the Refined spell keep the same Primary Factor, just for consistency.<br /> <br /> On another note. This makes much Practices obsolete in many cases, especially Ruling, Patterning and Unraveling. Are you excising them completely, or thinking of making them to something else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T19:58:28-08:00","id":1037016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033943-hack-refine?p=1036493#post1036493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting approach. However, I'd actually make the Refined spell keep the same Primary Factor, just for consistency.</div> </div> </div> </div>Usually that should be the case, but as demonstrated with Wield Flames Refined to Weaving, Duration as PSF is simply meaningless considering that it makes the effect Lasting to begin with. So any changes like that besides the Practice should be noted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1033943-hack-refine?p=1036493#post1036493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On another note. This makes much Practices obsolete in many cases, especially Ruling, Patterning and Unraveling. Are you excising them completely, or thinking of making them to something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, it just makes those Practices seem like less advanced versions of others, which is entirely the case for most Practices. I mean, you have Compelling, Ruling, Weaving, and Patterning, each one doing manipulation but in more advanced ways than the last.<br /> <br /> Although, now that you mention it, I did have an idea one time where instead of having 13 Practices, there would only be 4, Unveiling, Weaving, Threading, and Unraveling. They represented much more general effects, Unveiling was all about information gathering in all its forms, Weaving was all about manipulating whatever was in the Arcanum's purview, Threading was all about creation and bolstering, and Unraveling was all about destruction and weakening. Each of the original 13 Practices' effects would be emulated by the 4 (Unveiling did Knowing and Unveiling, Weaving did Compelling, Ruling, Veiling, Weaving, and Patterning, Threading did Shielding, Perfecting, and Making, and Unraveling did Fraying, Unraveling, and Unmaking). Each dot level in an Arcanum would grant further use in all 4 Practices at the same time, rather than giving more Practices to work with.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, it got really hard to come up with spells at higher dots for Unveiling and at lower dots for Threading and Unraveling, so it was a bit of a bust. Then reading about Reach and Creative Thaumaturgy in the development blogs made the idea obsolete.<br /> <br /> So I simply made Refine to get over Reach's soft limitation problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}